WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
One photo is all an AI face-swap tool needs to fake your face.

00:00:04.866 --> 00:00:08.552
Hi, I'm Aria Sharma, and FACADE was born at Cornell Tech's Summer

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:11.126
Innovation Intensives on Roosevelt Island.

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:14.962
It's an iPhone app that protects your photos before you share them,

00:00:15.012 --> 00:00:18.142
so AI face swaps have a harder time copying your face,

00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:20.666
for students and anyone who posts photos.

00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:22.365
Hi, I'm Catalina.

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:28.057
One in eight young people knew someone targeted with deepfake nudes as a minor.

00:00:28.107 --> 00:00:33.427
A Texas teen's ordinary photos became fake nudes, helping inspire the TAKE

00:00:33.477 --> 00:00:38.343
IT DOWN Act: platforms must now remove these fakes within 48 hours.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:40.607
But that's after the harm.

00:00:40.657 --> 00:00:43.583
We wanted protection before you post.

00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:44.916
I'm Sadie Hertzig.

00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:48.670
Face swaps turn your face into a 512-number identity code and paste

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.152
it onto someone else.

00:00:50.202 --> 00:00:54.400
Researchers at the University of Chicago and MIT built Fawkes and PhotoGuard,

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.944
which use tiny pixel changes to shield photos from face recognition and AI editing.

00:00:58.994 --> 00:01:03.883
We target InSwapper and SimSwap, models inside free apps like FaceFusion and Deep-Live-Cam.

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:08.035
A photo is a grid of pixels, each three numbers: red, green and blue.

00:01:08.085 --> 00:01:12.400
On your phone, FACADE nudges those color numbers by at most 5 out of 255,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.393
in about a minute, pushing the face's identity code away from you.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.948
Here's that layer, brightened 24 times.

00:01:18.998 --> 00:01:21.929
Swap the original, and the fake looks like her.

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:24.378
Swap the protected one: someone else.

00:01:24.428 --> 00:01:26.508
That's one hand-picked example.

00:01:26.558 --> 00:01:30.394
In 192 test swaps, 92 percent of SimSwap fakes stopped matching,

00:01:30.444 --> 00:01:32.683
but only 59 percent for InSwapper.

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:36.098
In the app, you pick a photo, tap Protect, compare,

00:01:36.148 --> 00:01:38.033
and run a face-swap test.

00:01:38.066 --> 00:01:41.756
And Get Help links to how the TAKE IT DOWN Act works and,

00:01:41.806 --> 00:01:45.723
if you still need help, how to reach your member of Congress,

00:01:45.773 --> 00:01:47.366
who's there to help.

00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:51.443
I'm Evelyn; the team brought me in to help with the phone engineering.

00:01:51.493 --> 00:01:56.376
PhotoGuard targets diffusion models like Stable Diffusion and DALL·E, which can repaint

00:01:56.426 --> 00:01:57.661
part of a photo.

00:01:57.711 --> 00:02:01.926
Our phone version, Mini PhotoGuard, isn't there yet: it takes six minutes,

00:02:01.976 --> 00:02:05.369
visibly changes the photo, and isn't proven to stop edits.

00:02:05.419 --> 00:02:09.274
The full version needs more engineering to run on a phone; for now,

00:02:09.324 --> 00:02:11.433
it runs on facadephotoshield.com.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.707
We ran hundreds of research experiments in Python and PyTorch to get FACADE working.

00:02:16.757 --> 00:02:20.665
The app is Swift, SwiftUI and Core ML; the site is TypeScript

00:02:20.715 --> 00:02:22.248
and Next.js on AWS.

00:02:22.298 --> 00:02:26.036
Codex and Claude Code were a huge help on the iPhone side;

00:02:26.086 --> 00:02:28.750
we couldn't have built it without them.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.186
Next, we need funding to train our own face-swap models,

00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:37.050
plus Mini PhotoGuard engineering, real social-media tests, and an App Store launch.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.835
As AI gets more powerful, protecting our digital identities matters more than ever.

00:02:41.885 --> 00:02:46.100
FACADE is our step toward making that protection accessible for everyone.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.216
FACADE tries to get ahead of the harm.

00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:50.266
Your photo.

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:52.761
Your choice.

00:02:52.811 --> 00:02:56.183
Thanks for watching!
